.Dd August 17, 2026
.Dt RUNLEVEL 8
.Os Sowa
.Sh NAME
.Nm runlevel
.Nd print the previous and current runlevel
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the runlevel the system was in before the current one and the runlevel
it is in now, separated by a space.
.Ql N
stands for
.Dq there was no previous one ,
which is what a machine that has been in the same runlevel since it booted
reports.
.Pp
It takes no options.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/run/initrunlevel" -compact
.It Pa /run/initrunlevel
where
.Xr init 8
records the runlevel.
System V read this out of utmp; glibc 2.42 removed the functions that wrote
utmp, so nothing on a Sowa system produces that record and
.Xr init 8
keeps a file of its own instead.
The output is unchanged.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A system whose runlevel cannot be read - which means
.Xr init 8
has not recorded one yet - prints
.Ql unknown
and exits 1.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ runlevel
N 3
.Ed
.Pp
The current runlevel alone, which is what a script wants:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
read -r previous current < <(runlevel)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr chkconfig 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr telinit 8
